> :quit

// A send that finds no method signals a `<no-applicable-method>`, which
// breaks like any unhandled condition. Its generic's dispatcher signals it,
// so the innermost frame is `area#dispatch`, and the break shows the
// generic and the classes and values of the arguments. `use-value` supplies
// the send's result, which must keep the generic's promise: 500 is outside
// `area`'s range, so the dispatcher signals a `<type-error>`, and 4 passes.
// Editing the sender and retrying its frame works as for any condition.

=== repl: a send that finds no method breaks with its condition

