// Methods are part of the runtime layout, which every code unit of a run
// shares, so a method added while a send waits cannot be installed under
// it: the edit is refused for this run and kept for the next one, which
// finds the new method.

=== repl: a method added under a failed send serves the next run

> :load tests/fixtures/break_loop/sends.loko
loaded tests/fixtures/break_loop/sends.loko (7 forms)
> :run main
break [1]: no handler for <no-applicable-method>; 3 frames suspended, nothing unwound
no applicable method: code=dispatch.no-applicable-method generic=area classes=(<square>) arguments=({<square>})
frames (innermost first):
  frame:0 area#dispatch  u0:f5
  frame:1 measure  u0:f0
  frame:2 main  u0:f1
restarts:
  restart:0 use-value(limited(<integer>, min: 0, max: 100))  the send returns this value instead, checked against its generic's result type
  restart:1 retry(frame)  call a frame's function again, with current definitions
  restart:2 abort()  unwind to top level, running cleanups
choose with :restart <n|name> [args...], or :edit <form-id> to fix a definition
> define method area(s :: <square>) => limited(<integer>, min: 0, max: 100)
>   s.side * s.side
> end;
! error: the edit is accepted for new runs but not installed here: cannot replace running code: the runtime layout changed (classes, slots or methods)
> :restart abort
